{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"selfish-brass-bluebottle","creation_channel":"cli","description":"On macOS, `pytest -q tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py::test_windows_noop` fails during the autouse `_one_engine_root` teardown. The test itself passes, then `tests/_engine_path.py::engine_root_of` calls `Path(path).resolve()` while `pathlib.Path` is still patched/aliased to `WindowsPath`, producing `NotImplementedError: cannot instantiate 'WindowsPath' on your system` for `\\\\Users\\\\joeoakhart...` paths.\n\nEvidence: the same solo command fails in both /Users/joeoakhart/alm-2340 and the shared /Users/joeoakhart/rebar checkout at current origin/main, so this is a pre-existing baseline validation blocker rather than a child-material regression.\n\nAcceptance: isolate/restore the WindowsPath monkeypatch or make the engine-root guard robust so the solo test and make verify pass on macOS without weakening foreign-engine detection.","id":"f46c-8a93-2eb9-4913","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Mac baseline verify fails after WindowsPath noop test"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789023179566795001,"uuid":"b40abef3-c978-480f-8246-62a2ab2b4bdd"}